<http://data.silknow.org/object/7766b4f2-d878-3d5d-9af8-36e7485588dd>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A pair of leather gloves with applied red silk on gauntlet and metal thread embroidery & fringe. The design consists of cartouche devices alternating with conventional plant forms. The border on three sides is filled with a repeating curved floral stem. There is a looped fringe of gold thread."@en , "Silver and silver-gilt embroidery and fringing decorate the gauntlet of this leather glove from the early 17th century.  Red satin has been appliquéd to the leather and covered with silver purl (tiny coils of very fine metal wire) in a stylised pattern of leaves and flowers.\nGloves were a popular choice of gift in the 17th century.  It was customary to present the monarch with a pair at New Year, and gloves were also frequently exchanged as wedding gifts."@en , "Silver thread embroidery on leather; England; 1610-1625."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/d9ba5af3-bbf1-3d5a-b64d-bf8533cb701d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/1bcfc321-c1f4-3b1d-be83-708d02e80701> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/2f63ef40-dc66-39d9-97e4-d4aa354f8d06> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ac10bcbf-06f9-3990-858c-410e4ccfa729> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/27f4b2cd-a78f-36ac-8c4f-4180f7c9bd2f> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Silver and silver-gilt embroidery and fringing decorate the gauntlet of this leather glove from the early 17th century.  Red satin has been appliquéd to the leather and covered with silver purl (tiny coils of very fine metal wire) in a stylised pattern of leaves and flowers.\nGloves were a popular choice of gift in the 17th century.  It was customary to present the monarch with a pair at New Year, and gloves were also frequently exchanged as wedding gifts."@en , "Silver thread embroidery on leather; England; 1610-1625."@en , "A pair of leather gloves with applied red silk on gauntlet and metal thread embroidery & fringe. The design consists of cartouche devices alternating with conventional plant forms. The border on three sides is filled with a repeating curved floral stem. There is a looped fringe of gold thread."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/7766b4f2-d878-3d5d-9af8-36e7485588dd/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/7766b4f2-d878-3d5d-9af8-36e7485588dd/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.154&A-1930" ;
